{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-topological-invariance}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aec90f92e25b0b047b91f988aaf49ed3c7f0665f132f3403c92d36e40a289d3d", "source_text": "Topological invariance of the small <ACCENT_0001>tale site", "source_text_hash": "sha256:01df0f8d333ebdb6a447191711917ef610366e45745b7545e3d04eeacdd0ae41", "unit_id": "tag:04DY:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'E", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$X_\\etale \\cong Y_\\etale$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{etale-theorem-remarkable-equivalence}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1ba186c8edaa49f12f4406445a13e5e8c7001b0505463a24b8e08647de943108", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d23e16388d7a9027ad07cdbdd6e505c5e5095cf7e9e077a2442f98c14d2c09f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the following theorem we show that the small <ACCENT_0001>tale site is a topological\ninvariant in the following sense: If <MATH_0001> is a morphism of schemes\nwhich is a universal homeomorphism, then <MATH_0002>\nas sites. This improves the result of\n<ACCENT_0002>tale Morphisms, Theorem <REF_0001>.\nWe first prove the result for morphisms and then we state the result\nfor categories.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7be8b6cbb451fdafbe66a4ab6850807c062c072a1e74e5bd5bd6c59966ea8a7", "unit_id": "tag:04DY:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "04DY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S' \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$X'$", "MATH_0006": "$Y'$", "MATH_0007": "$S'$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\Mor_S(Y, X) \\longrightarrow \\Mor_{S'}(Y', X')\n$$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-etale-topological}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a781e27abc5756703cdfc5bd5a962969ec8f6d15970d5f25ae282baf03a7c58b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c49880f9793a3de1692538ca12d5fd56c63509e819b9f57591940fe6a482f400", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be two schemes over a base scheme <MATH_0003>. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a universal homeomorphism.\nDenote <MATH_0005> (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0006>) the base change to <MATH_0007>.\nIf <MATH_0008> is <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0009>, then the map\n<MATH_0010>\nis bijective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b49cd5d7fd991ae805f0f71c4ecc7dcd846bfd0ec670a9f86ec33587d4fae19", "unit_id": "tag:0BTY:statement"}
